MyGo patch 0006 (Auralink): prereleases, a beta channel of an update
URL.

Apps whose updates are served from updates.url only ever have one
channel. An app with a beta channel needs its users who opt in to get
prereleases (1.3.0-beta.1), and the others not to.

- updates.prereleases (mygo.json, mygo.config.ts; needs url, not s3):
  the files of a version with a pre-release part point into the beta/
  directory of url (the manifest's URLs); a release's stay in url. The
  server publishes them there and keeps the beta channel's manifest the
  newest version of both channels (-upload does not). Builds make delta
  updates from the newest version of both channels (each channel's
  manifest, then the versions they list), so that a user on the last
  beta and one on the last release both get a delta of the next version.
- The build links in the beta channel's manifest beside the releases'
  (packageUpdateBetaFeed). mygo.Updater.SetPrereleases(on) /
  Prereleases(): with it on, Check reads the beta channel's manifest and,
  when that fails, the releases'. Updates never go back.
- mygo.ErrNotPublished: Check's error wraps it when the feed's manifest
  is not found (no version published yet), and the updater plugin shows
  "up to date" for it instead of an error.
- docs/updates.md "Beta channel", docs/configuration.md.

Tests: TestUpdaterPrereleases (channels, a fix after a beta of the next
version, no downgrade, the beta channel down, nothing published),
TestWriteDeltasPrereleases, TestUpdatesConfig, TestNotPublished (plugin).
