+## Beta channel
+
+Apps whose updates are served from `url` can offer prereleases, such as
+`1.3.0-beta.1`, to the users who opt in: a beta channel. Set
+`prereleases` in `updates`,
+
+```ts
+updates: {
+  publicKey: "…",
+  url: "https://downloads.example.com/my-app",
+  prereleases: true,
+},
+```
+
+and the files of a version with a pre-release part point into the
+`beta/` directory of `url` (the manifest's URLs); a release's stay in
+`url`. Publish a beta's files in `beta/`, and a release's in `url` and its
+manifest in `beta/` too unless a newer beta is there: the beta channel's
+manifest is always the newest version of both channels. Your server or
+release pipeline does that; `-upload` does not, and `prereleases` cannot be
+used with `s3`.
+
+The app chooses at run time, for example from a preference:
+
+```go
+mygo.Updater.SetPrereleases(settings.Beta)
+```
+
+`Check` then reads the beta channel's manifest, and offers the next beta
+or release, whichever is newer; when it fails, `Check` falls back to the
+releases'. Updates never go back: a user who turns prereleases off on a
+beta waits for a release newer than it. The choice is not saved: set it
+each time the app starts, before the first check. A feed without a
+version yet makes `Check` return an error wrapping
+`mygo.ErrNotPublished`, which the updater plugin shows as up to date.
+
+[Delta updates](#delta-updates) of a build with `prereleases` come from
+the newest version of both channels, then the versions their manifests
+list: a user on the last beta and a user of the last release both
+download a delta of the next version, whichever channel it is in.
+
 ## Delta updates
 
 As with Sparkle, apps download only what changed since their version,
